# Claude Code agent runtime locks — session-scoped, never source
**/scheduled_tasks.lock

# OMC agent runtime state — session-scoped, never source.
# An .omc/ below the repo root is always accidental: the hook writes one into
# whatever directory a command happened to cd into (frontend/, workers/,
# frontend/src/). Ignore every .omc/, then re-admit the repo-root one so its
# authored artefacts (plans, research, design, prd) stay tracked.
**/.omc/
!/.omc/
/.omc/sessions/
/.omc/state/
/.omc/project-memory.json
# ...including a nested .omc/ under an authored subtree (the re-admit above
# would otherwise let e.g. .omc/research/ux-audit/.omc/state/ back in).
/.omc/**/.omc/

# Same story for a stray .claude/ below the repo root.
**/.claude/
!/.claude/
.claude/worktrees/

# Supabase CLI temp
supabase/.temp/

# Scripts secrets
scripts/.env

